# Story 18: 35+ Agentic Tools (60s)
# Hook: Your AI co-pilot comes loaded with 35+ tools -- file ops, search, git, and more.
# Duration: 60s
# Source: story-18-agentic-tools.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 8

[00:00.0 --> 00:04.0]
Start rysh -- you land in shell mode.

[00:04.0 --> 00:08.0]
Double-press Escape to enter prompt mode. The prompt changes to < -- now you're talking to AI.

[00:08.0 --> 00:22.0]
Ask the AI to show its full toolkit. 35+ tools covering file ops, search, git, web, and more.

[00:22.0 --> 00:28.0]
File read, file write, glob search, grep, bash execution, git operations, web fetch, context store -- the list goes on.

[00:28.0 --> 00:38.0]
Now put a tool to work -- read the first 10 lines of the nearest README.

[00:38.0 --> 00:48.0]
The AI calls its file_read tool behind the scenes and returns the content right in your terminal.

[00:48.0 --> 00:55.0]
Press Escape to drop back to shell mode.

[00:55.0 --> 01:00.0]
35+ tools, zero setup. Your AI is ready to work.

